From b0473945918d77ecd3dafb0411838495a681c539 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:43:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add scenario 5: visibility and hard kill during publication

Raised by Tim Urista on the article: os.replace is atomic per file, not for the
set of reports. shared/crash_scenario.py runs a concurrent reader (observe) or
a SIGKILL between the two publications (kill) on a stack and reports what is
left, what the next run does, and the state after the stack's recovery command.
shared/make_probe_dag.py widens the Airflow window so it can be hit on purpose.
Results measured in a Linux sandbox, not on the EC2 machine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
